<%# Self-hosted Latin subsets (#90; built by script/build_fonts.py, OFL). No
    font is preloaded: a 51 KB preload shared the slow-4G bandwidth with the
    render-blocking CSS and put LCP at 2.1 to 2.4 s on every page, a few
    hundredths from the 2.5 s budget as /companies grew. Without the preload a
    font-display: swap serif arrives after first paint and moves the page
    (layout shift 0.25 on /companies in CI), so Roboto Serif and Roboto Mono
    are font-display: optional: a font that is not ready within the first
    moments waits for the next page, so nothing moves. The wordmark is an SVG,
    so Anton loads only where a display heading uses it. %>
<style>
  @font-face { font-family: "Roboto Serif"; src: url("<%= asset_path "roboto-serif-latin.woff2" %>") format("woff2"); font-weight: 400 700; font-style: normal; font-display: optional; }
  @font-face { font-family: "Roboto Mono"; src: url("<%= asset_path "roboto-mono-latin.woff2" %>") format("woff2"); font-weight: 400 500; font-style: normal; font-display: optional; }
  @font-face { font-family: "Anton"; src: url("<%= asset_path "anton-latin.woff2" %>") format("woff2"); font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-display: swap; }
</style>
